<!--Post: 9510--><!--Time: 1109542326-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9510"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think we need comments like that. After all, Steve Huff is connected, and he came up with those blog replies from close to where the letter was postmarked from, and in the correct time frame, I believe. I still like that comment made by some wag about Mark Fuhrman&#39;s book. &#34;Well, The Spokane PD&#39;s guy is on death row, Fuhrman&#39;s is still on the loose.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9510-->
<!--Post: 9775--><!--Time: 1109636626-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9775"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR> <BR>I was not laughing at YOU really.  I have a file of all your posts regarding your clues and breakthroughs and you were so ofof base it is - well - funny.  Course I was way off base too.  The difference is that you went on the record with your Google hypothesis.  It just doesn&#39;t work that way Skov.  Chalk it up to experience for the next time.  And if I were to have promoted my belefs to I would have as much egg on my face as you do - as we all do. <BR> <BR>NO winners here - except LE. <BR> <BR>Cheers <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9775-->
<!--Post: 9778--><!--Time: 1109637068-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9778"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov may have been offbase on a few things but if I had a law firm and Skov was looking for a job I would hire her as a paralegal, no reumé needed. Talk about a researcher!  <BR>Or if i was running for political office I would hate to have my opponent hire skov to look into my background. She&#39;d find stuff even I had forgot about.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
